@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Find your order details - Lively Help Center";
    ViewData["CategorySlug"] = "Buying";
    ViewData["SubCategorySlug"] = "Buying items";
    ViewData["HeroTitle"] = "Find your order details";
    ViewData["HeroStyle"] = "background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0.4), rgba(0,0,0,0.4)), url('/help_centre_img/help_area/help_centre_hero_bg.png');";
    ViewData["IsArticle"] = true;
}

<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>While getting help with an order, you may need to share order details like your Order ID or tracking number. Here's how to find them.</p>

        <p><strong>Open your order details:</strong></p>
        <ol>
            <li>Open the Lively app or go to <a href="https://lively.com">lively.com</a></li>
            <li>Go to <strong>Activity</strong></li>
            <li>Select the <strong>Purchases</strong> tab</li>
            <li>Choose the order you need help with</li>
        </ol>

        <p>From the order details page, you can view and copy:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Tracking number</strong> – select <strong>'Tracking'</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Order ID</strong> – a 9-digit number (example: 123456789)</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Need help with an order? <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Home">Learn how to contact Lively support.</a></p>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>80 out of 145 found this helpful</span>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>